"priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the reversibility mechanism for deletions: require the ADR/children to sequence migrate-then-delete (expand-contract) with an explicit back-out (re-add binding) if a missed consumer surfaces in CI.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'No old private binding remains solely for internal compatibility'","AC1 requires the ADR define 'atomic consumer migration' but not a rollback mechanism","No back-out plan for a deletion that breaks a missed dynamic/string/monkeypatch consumer"],"finding":"The plan deletes old private bindings (a destructive change) but specifies no explicit rollback/back-out path if a consumer is missed after deletion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0cec6aa5b42e568b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC2/AC3; Approach","norm_id":"nc0c57cdd86be6b83","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A string-based or monkeypatch consumer is missed by the census; deletion breaks it at runtime with no stated recovery"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC1 or the Approach: deletions occur only after consumer migration is verified in CI, and the child PR is revertable as the back-out path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion covering the SDC3 alias migrations (or state they fall under AC2's 'enumerated internal shim'), and expand the 'SDC3' acronym on first use.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6987,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Body names 'approved SDC3 alias migrations' as owned work","No AC explicitly references alias migrations distinct from 'internal shim' consumers","'SDC3' acronym is never expanded"],"finding":"The 'SDC3 alias migrations' named as a distinct deliverable in Child Decomposition has no covering acceptance criterion, and 'SDC3' is undefined.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb8b49030c13dea5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Child Decomposition: 'The LLM/workflow shard also owns approved SDC3 alias migrations'; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n042a1fbc77f5dda2","priority":0.2513,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor completes shim migrations but leaves SDC3 alias migrations unverified because no AC gates them"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either fold aliases explicitly into AC2/AC3 wording, or add an AC: 'Approved SDC3 alias assignments are migrated to their canonical binding and the alias is removed.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Have the ADR classification criteria explicitly separate compatibility-only shims (deletable after consumer migration) from structurally-load-bearing re-exports (acyclicity seams, monkeypatch-identity `is` seams, module-size-cap facades), and require the deletion step to prove no import cycle / identity-seam / size-cap regression before removing a binding.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Their only beneficiaries are repository imports, strings, and monkeypatch targets, so they create a second binding without protecting a public compatibility contract.'","src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:17-27 — 'This module is a LEAF with NO module-level rebar import: it keeps the re-export in rebar._config_sources acyclic ... a monkeypatch.setattr on that module still steers this code. Binding them eagerly at import time is the exact regression the sibling config.py split shipped.'","Numerous tests assert re-export object IDENTITY (`is`) and load-bearing status, e.g. tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py:152 ('workflow_ops re-exports it'), tests/unit/test_lock_age_ceiling.py:303 ('lock.py re-exports moved names, defeating patch targets')","ABSENCE: the ADR child's exception list is named ('valid exceptions') but the plan does not name the structural (acyclicity / monkeypatch-identity / module-size) class of non-compatibility re-export as an input to that classification."],"finding":"The core deletion step ('migrate all consumers, then delete the old private binding') has an unhandled edge case: some re-exports in the codebase exist for structural reasons (keeping an import graph acyclic, preserving monkeypatch-identity `is` seams, or staying under module-size caps) rather than for consumer compatibility. Deleting such a binding after its enumerable consumers migrate can reintroduce an import cycle, break a monkeypatch-identity assertion, or push a module over its size cap — even though no compatibility contract was violated. The plan's classification ('only beneficiaries are repository imports, strings, and monkeypatch targets') and its deletion step do not distinguish compatibility-only shims from structurally-load-bearing re-exports.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbe4dc7d1e0da0c5e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / AC line 3 ('No old private binding remains solely for internal compatibility')","norm_id":"nf1d51d1377a14890","priority":0.1675,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A migration child moves every import site off rebar._config_sources.X, then deletes the re-export, reintroducing the import cycle config.py was split to avoid.","A child deletes a re-export that a test pins via `is` for monkeypatch identity, silently no-oping a patch instead of failing loudly."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the ADR child's policy, add a named exception class for structural re-exports and require each migration child, before deleting a binding, to confirm (a) the binding is not the acyclic-import seam, (b) no test pins its object identity via monkeypatch, and (c) removal does not push the defining module over the size cap.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"ae58f2ed571053ad","material_parts":{"children":["64f2160c472df751",5],"description":["90b1b747ed20b45e",1540],"description_boxes":["1a0f564ddc603945",0],"file_impact":["003ffa614d5e4a28",0],"file_impact_scope":["d5cf63ac07401a0c",2],"ticket_id":["56e05d9b33ec88c5",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":94889,"cache_write_tokens":48230,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":10845.5,"input_tokens":164379,"llm_calls":22,"llm_ms":204872.7,"output_tokens":14256,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":228157.0,"verify_requests":18},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":